course: dictionary
lesson: 731
title: Context clues: basement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A basement is a room or floor of a building that is partly or fully under the ground. You can work out what it means from the words around it. «The safest place in a tornado is a basement or storm shelter» tells you that a basement is a place to hide from a storm.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «a small inside room or a basement on the lowest floor, away from windows.» The words lowest floor and away from windows show that a basement is down low, with no windows. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a room under the ground on the lowest floor" still makes sense.
explain: Words change from place to place. In North America people often say basement, but in the UK and Australia they may say cellar for a similar room. Both words describe a room below ground, so if you meet one you do not know, the context can help.
explain: Stories use basements too. A basement in a spooky tale can feel dark and mysterious, but in real houses it is often used for storage, laundry or a playroom. The context tells you which picture the author wants you to see.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Basement» means a room or floor of a building that is partly or fully under the ground.
fact: In North America, basements are common and are used for storage, laundry, playrooms or furnaces.
fact: In the UK and Australia, people more often say «cellar».
fact: In a tornado, a basement is a safe place, but it can flood in heavy rain.
exercise: «In a tornado the safest place is a small inside room or a basement on the lowest floor, away from windows.» What is a basement? | A tall tower on the roof | A room with the biggest windows | A small garden shed | *A room or floor under the ground
exercise: In «an inside room or a basement on the lowest floor», which word tells you a basement is low down? | inside | room | *lowest | small
exercise: Chloe's family keeps their washing machine in the basement. What is a basement often used for? | *Laundry | Growing tall trees | Swimming in the ocean | Flying kites
test: Some people in the UK say which word for a room under the ground? | Attic | *Cellar | Garage | Balcony
test: In a spooky story, the basement is dark and mysterious. What does the context suggest? | Only for birds to nest in | *Dark and mysterious, a place that might scare you | Bright, sunny and full of flowers | Empty of all rooms
exam: Why is a basement safe in a tornado but still a risk in heavy rain? | It is made of glass | It is high up in the sunshine | It has no walls at all | *It is under the ground and away from windows, but it can flood
